    "body": "@jonathandturner : I understand from cli.rs that NuShell uses starship::context::Context::new_with_dir to specify the directory for the prompt. \r\nTo better understand the behavior with the current version  0.41.3, I'd love to have your hindsight on the following: \r\n- does NuShell change the current working directory when executing cd? ( i.e. what std::env::current_dir() returns?)\r\n- does NuShell update the PWD env var when executing cd? (i.e. std::env::var(\"PWD\"))\r\n- does NuShell's starship config change the default value for use_logical_path? (seems not but... never knowns)\r\n\r\n@davidkna & @jonathandturner : I tested NuShell with #1209 and it fixes this NuShell issue (as it is not dependant on the value of PWD or std::env::current_dir(). Only a very minor code change is necessary in NuShell (adding one None argument to starship::context::Context::new_with_dir)\r\n\r\n@jonathandturner : I did not know about NuShell and, as a Powershell user, I can say that I am really loving NuShell so far and really looking into it now! It's GREAT!\r\n ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
